{"docstring":"Milestone R2 acceptance: Every suite app starts and works in the VM;\nglyphs and fonts render on kmscon; power actions work.","hash":"101840b6d03fbea7e7e9ab3a1d8cd43b571340f23f4862b15ed0b78c4eeda2ee","inherits":["libspec.spec_types.Requirement"],"is_template":false,"ref":"spec.milestones.R2FullSuiteValidation","type":"component"}
{"docstring":"Milestone R3 acceptance: Regular installs in BIOS and UEFI VMs and on\npizzabox via BMC; tag v1.1.0.","hash":"7d7ac19688485cb9052162657c6aaa1094893647521d0c3bd637c0c23eb23523","inherits":["libspec.spec_types.Requirement"],"is_template":false,"ref":"spec.milestones.R3RegularInstallAndHardware","type":"component"}
{"docstring":"USER-STORY: LIVE-TRY\n\nAnyone can boot the ISO live from USB or virtual media into tetron-wm\nwithout installing anything.\n\nPriority: medium.\nAcceptance: live boot assertions pass in BIOS and UEFI VMs.","hash":"914453c3f005b23327f81ce0a42ee1cab67ba462c6c071a046d1e5cefe5c8aec","inherits":["libspec.user_story.UserStory","libspec.spec_types.Feature"],"is_template":false,"ref":"spec.product.LiveTry","type":"component"}
{"docstring":"USER-STORY: REGULAR-FULL-INSTALL\n\nA user boots the Regular edition live ISO, tries it, and installs a fully\nprovisioned TetronOS: kmscon console, tetron-wm desktop, the whole app\nsuite, tetron mesh, all hardware firmware, offline.\n\nPriority: high (end goal, follows v1).\nAcceptance: milestones R0 to R3.","hash":"f52d73bc7d62f2a968a87d667cd7bef1199e33bc7cfa4eb71eb32cb67f249b14","inherits":["libspec.user_story.UserStory","libspec.spec_types.Feature"],"is_template":false,"ref":"spec.product.RegularFullInstall","type":"component"}
{"docstring":"USER-STORY: SERVER-BMC-INSTALL\n\nAn operator attaches a small TetronOS Server ISO to a machine through its\nBMC virtual media and installs it remotely, with no one at the keyboard.\n\nPriority: high (v1).\nUser journey: attach ISO via BMC -> boot on serial or BMC KVM -> unattended\nor TUI install to disk -> reboot -> the machine is on the tetron mesh.\nAcceptance: verified in VMs first, then on pizzabox through its BMC\n(milestone M9). The ISO stays under the Server size budget.","hash":"df037f61ad5a029e16413a69f4ba85e052dbf0c62b6d482f3e4d94e700b3c214","inherits":["libspec.user_story.UserStory","libspec.spec_types.Feature"],"is_template":false,"ref":"spec.product.ServerBmcInstall","type":"component"}
